-- title:
--   Weight-zero series are e-th expansions modulo X₀X₁-π
-- statement:
--   Let $W$ be a commutative ring and $\pi \in W$ an element such that $W$ is precomplete for the ideal $(\pi)$ generated by $\pi$, and such that $\pi$-divisibility separates points: every $x \in W$ divisible by $\pi^n$ for all $n \in \mathbb{N}$ is $0$. Let $e$ be a natural number with $e \neq 0$, and let $F$ be a formal power series in two variables over $W$, i.e. $F \in$ `MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) W`, whose support consists of weight-zero monomials in the following sense: for every exponent function $d : \mathrm{Fin}\ 2 \to_{f} \mathbb{N}$ with $\mathrm{coeff}_d F \neq 0$ one has $e \mid d(0) - d(1)$ as integers. Then there exists $G \in$ `MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) W` such that $F$ and the $e$-fold expansion of $G$, obtained by substituting $X_0^e, X_1^e$ for the two variables, have the same image under the quotient map `mk π` onto $W[[X_0,X_1]]/(X_0X_1 - C(\pi))$; that is, $F \equiv G(X_0^e, X_1^e)$ modulo the principal ideal generated by $X_0X_1 - \pi$.
--
--   This is the surjectivity half of the identification of the image of $W[[u,v]]/(uv-\pi^e) \to W[[X_0,X_1]]/(X_0X_1-\pi)$, $u \mapsto X_0^e$, $v \mapsto X_1^e$, with the classes of power series supported in monomials $X_0^aX_1^b$ satisfying $a \equiv b \pmod e$ — a root-of-unity-free form of the statement that the $\mu_e$-invariants of the crossing model are again a crossing model. It is used by [`ModularCurve.UVCrossingModel.exists_powMap_range_eq_fixedPoints`](thm.html#ModularCurve.UVCrossingModel.exists_powMap_range_eq_fixedPoints), which identifies that image with a fixed-point set.
-- source:
